  "wikitext": "Galactic coordinate includes few ranks: [[galactic coordinate i|I]], [[galactic coordinate ii|II]], [[galactic coordinate iii|III]], [[galactic coordinate iv|IV]] and [[galactic coordinate v|V]].\n\nYou cost this when you go on [[Galactic Expedition|galactic expedition]]s. This can be collected by [[research]]ing.\n\nDifferent difficulty on the galactic expeditions has different value, all shown in the table below.\n{|class=\"wikitable\"\n! Difficulty\n! Galactic Coordinate\n! [[Rocket fuel]]\n! Success chance -- Base value\n! Damage on Failure ([[Space station parts]])\n|-\n| I (1) || [[galactic coordinate i|Galactic Coordinate I]] || 100 || 80% || 100\n|-\n| II (2) || [[galactic coordinate ii|Galactic Coordinate II]] || 200 || 60% || 200\n|-\n| III (3) || [[galactic coordinate iii|Galactic Coordinate III]] || 300 || 40% || 300\n|-\n| IV (4) || [[galactic coordinate iv|Galactic Coordinate IV]] || 400 || 20% || 400\n|-\n| V (5) || [[galactic coordinate v|Galactic Coordinate V]] || 500 || 0% || 500\n|}\n\nEvery level of expeditions all cost same value of coordinate (1) and [[rocket]] (1).\n\nFailure may either give you the rocket back or the rocket having a chance to be destroyed.",
